# Allowlist principle: EVERYTHING is ignored, only explicitly opted-in config is versioned.
# Why: this directory also holds .credentials.json (OAuth token), projects/ (complete
# session transcripts), history.jsonl and assorted caches. A denylist would be a leak
# risk with every new file Claude Code drops in here. Under this allowlist, anything
# new is ignored by default.
#
# NEVER force with `git add -f`. If something is missing, add a ! rule here instead.

*

# --- Versioned configuration ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
# Global CLAUDE.md: carries the rules that hold across projects (language, honesty,
# confidence gate, tests, handover). Anything project-specific belongs in that
# project's own CLAUDE.md, not here.
!CLAUDE.md
# Imported by CLAUDE.md as @language.md, so it loads at session start. Carries both
# language axes; switching means replacing this file and settings.json.
!language.md
!settings.json
# Binds the clean filter to settings.json (see scripts/strip-volatile-settings.mjs):
# model and effort are written by the UI and do not belong in the history.
!.gitattributes

# Public-repository furniture
!LICENSE
!CONTRIBUTING.md
!SECURITY.md

# Statusline
!ccstatusline-config.json
!statusline-command.sh
!statusline-wrapper.cmd
!statusline-wrapper.sh

# Own skills — un-ignore the directory first, so git looks inside it. These rules
# reach recursively, at any depth. Everything invocable lives here: what used to be
# commands/ moved in on 2026-08-27, one mechanism instead of two.
!skills/
!skills/**

# CI. Runs only the three tests that check the repository's content; settings-hygiene
# checks this machine's .git/config and stays local — the workflow says why.
!.github/
!.github/**

# The Bash guard: three "never" rules from CLAUDE.md as a gate rather than a request,
# because a command has no file for a path-scoped rule to hang on. Fail-open by design,
# so tests/bash-guard.test.mjs is what proves it still bites.
!hooks/
!hooks/**

# Path-scoped rules — sections of CLAUDE.md that only hold for some projects.
# Frontmatter `paths` makes them load when a matching file is read and cost nothing
# otherwise; measured to work at user scope on 2.1.245, see docs/context-budget.md.
!rules/
!rules/**

# Tests of the workflow harnesses (node tests/<file>, no dependencies)
!tests/
!tests/**

# Templates to copy into a new project (carried over from claude-setup)
!project-template/
!project-template/**

# Own notes and documentation about the Claude setup itself
!docs/
!docs/**

# Reusable scripts that commands call (claude-md-audit and others)
!scripts/
!scripts/**
